---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACT, MEMBERSHIPS } from '../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'About us', url: '/about/' }];
const verifiedMemberships = MEMBERSHIPS.filter((m) => m.verified);
---

<Page
  title="About John Bald Funeral Directors, Dunbar"
  heading="About us"
  description="John Bald Funeral Directors has cared for families in Dunbar and East Lothian for over 50 years. Independent, family-run, and part of the A & A Doyle family."
  standfirst="Over fifty years in Dunbar, three sets of hands, and the same idea running through all of it."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p>
    John Bald opened this business in Dunbar more than fifty years ago. When he retired in
    2001 he passed it to Ian and Elizabeth Torrance, who looked after East Lothian
    families for another twenty years and built the reputation the name still carries.
  </p>

  <p>
    In December 2022 it came to us — Awdri and Allan Doyle. Ian could have sold to one of
    the national chains. He chose not to. He wanted the business to stay in independent
    hands, run by people who would answer their own telephone, and we were glad to be
    asked.
  </p>

  <h2>Bruce Robertson</h2>
  <p>
    Bruce manages our funeral home in Dunbar and looks after families here day to day. If
    you telephone us or call in, he is most likely the person you will deal with, from the
    first conversation through to the funeral itself and whatever follows it.
  </p>

  <h2>Awdri and Allan Doyle</h2>
  <p>
    Awdri grew up in it. Her parents were funeral directors in Gorebridge, and although
    she spent her teens certain she wanted nothing to do with the job, she found her way
    back to it after starting a family. She trained in 2004 and, with Allan, opened
    A & A Doyle in Galashiels in 2012. She is also a trained organist, and played at
    funerals for years before she started arranging them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Allan and Awdri lived and worked in Haddington and North Berwick for many years, and
    knew John Bald himself before he retired. They are not strangers to this county.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    The rule we run the business by is a simple one, and Awdri's: <em>do everything for
    your families as if they were your own.</em>
  </p>
  <p>
    In practice that means the telephone is answered by one of us, not a call centre.
    It means we will give you as much time as you want and no more than you want. It
    means we will tell you what things cost before you ask. And it means we will not
    push you toward anything — our job is to lay out the options honestly and then do
    whatever you decide.
  </p>

  <Callout title="There should be no rules about funerals">
    <p>
      Some families want the full traditional funeral. Some want twenty minutes and no
      fuss. Some want a willow coffin and the Proclaimers. All of it is fine. The only
      thing we hold to is the dignity of the person who has died — beyond that, it is
      your funeral to shape.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Part of a family of independents</h2>
  <p>
    John Bald Funeral Directors is part of {SITE.parentCompany}, alongside A & A Doyle in
    Galashiels and Herkes Funeral Directors in Gorebridge. Three funeral homes, one
    family, and no shareholders to answer to.
  </p>
  <p>
    Being part of a small group means we can call on each other for cover, share vehicles
    and staff when a family needs more than one funeral home can provide, and keep our
    costs lower than we could alone. What it does not mean is head office. Decisions
    about your funeral are made here in Dunbar.
  </p>

  {
    verifiedMemberships.length > 0 && (
      <>
        <h2>Our memberships</h2>
        <ul>
          {verifiedMemberships.map((m) => (
            <li>
              {m.name} — {m.abbr} member number {m.number}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </>
    )
  }

  <h2>Where we work</h2>
  <p>
    Dunbar and the surrounding villages, across East Lothian to East Linton, Haddington,
    North Berwick and Gullane, and south into Berwickshire — Eyemouth, Duns, Coldstream
    and the villages between. If you are outside that and would still like us, ask.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p>
      Come in whenever you like, or telephone{' '}
      <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a>. There is
      never a charge for a conversation.
    </p>
  </Callout>
</Page>
